<body style="height: auto; min-height: auto;">Ref: {{{Case.Case_Number__c}}}<br />
<br />
Hi {{{Case.First_Name__c}}},&nbsp;<br />
&nbsp;<br />
<strong>RE: File Reference {{{Case.Baggage_File_Reference__c}}}</strong><br />
&nbsp;<br />
Thank you for reaching out to the Qantas Customer Care team.<br />
<br />
We want our customers to have a smooth and seamless journey every time they fly with us, so I'm sorry to hear that your baggage didn’t arrive and for any inconvenience this has caused you.<br />
<br />
I wanted to assure you that we’re making every effort to locate your baggage and will let you know as soon as it has been successfully located and ready for delivery.<br />
<br />
Baggage can be delayed for multiple reasons such as, operational issues, weight and balance requirements, weather, enhanced security checks or Airport infrastructure.&nbsp; Due to these complexities, we have not been able to pinpoint the specific reason in your case.<br />
<br />
<strong>Next steps</strong><br />
<br />
While we work hard to find your baggage, we’ll need you to download and complete the <a href="https://www.qantas.com/content/dam/qantas/pdfs/fly/baggage/qantas-lost-damaged-baggage-form.pdf">Claim for Lost/Damaged Baggage Questionnaire</a>&nbsp;and email it back to us. Please include photocopies of the following documents:
<ul>
	<li>Your passenger ticket or if your ticket was electronic, your E-Ticket itinerary/receipt;</li>
	<li>Your baggage receipts given to you at check in;</li>
	<li>Photographic identification;</li>
	<li>Proof of purchase (if you are providing receipts as proof of purchase then original receipts must be provided)</li>
</ul>
<br />
Don’t hesitate to call us if you have any concerns or questions.</body>
